sentences.l:
So having spoken, beneath her feet she bound her fair sandals,
immortal, golden, which used to bear her both over the water
and over the boundless earth, together with the breaths of the wind;

And she went, darting down from the peaks of Olympus,
and stood in the land of Ithaca at the forecourt of Odysseus,
upon the threshold of the courtyard;

They, then,
with draughts-pieces before the doors were delighting their heart,
sitting on the hides of cattle which they themselves had killed;

And hand-water a handmaid poured over them, bringing it in a pitcher,
a fine golden one, over a silver basin,
for washing;

But when of drink and of food they had put away desire,
the suitors, then other things were a care in their minds,
song and dancing;

But as it is, he has perished so, by an evil fate, and there is no
warmth of comfort for us, even if someone of men upon the earth
says that he will come;
